# Copy this to ~/.config/standup/telegram.env — OUTSIDE the repository — and
# fill it in. Nothing in here is read from the repository itself, and nothing
# with a real value in it should ever be committed.
#
# Override the location with STANDUP_CONFIG_DIR.

# From @BotFather, when you create the bot.
#
# The placeholders are short and dull on purpose. This file is committed, and
# test_privacy.rb fails on anything here that looks like a real credential —
# both a bot-token shape and any long value assigned to a name ending in TOKEN.
# A realistic-looking example would fail its own repository's test. They are
# also plain shell assignments, because the script sources this file: no
# spaces, no angle brackets.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=replace-me

# The chat the standup is sent to. Your own user id for a private standup, or
# a group id, which is negative.
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=replace-me

# The publisher also reads ~/.config/standup/wip-token, a file holding just the
# wip.co API key. It is only needed if you publish to wip.co.
